  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Delhi Administration vs Vishwa Nath Khera. on 2 May, 2023 Bench: Abhay S. Oka, Rajesh Bindal Item No.8 Court No.17 Section Ii-C S U P R E M E C O U R T O F I N D I A Record Of Proceedings",
    "facts": "An application for leave to prefer appeal was filed before the Delhi Administration vs Vishwa Nath Khera. Therefore, the benefit of doubt was granted to the respondent.",
    "arguments": "This Court by a judgment dated 24th April, 2018 in Criminal Appeal No.625 of 2018 in the case of Delhi Administration v. Vidya Gupta took a view that there was no reason for the Court to even refer to the contents of report of the Public Analyst, as the law enjoins the Court to only consider the contents of the certificate of Director.",
